/-!
# Chains of generating functions and the cyclic discrete action

Let `S_0, …, S_(N-1)`, `N ≥ 1`, be real functions on `Q × Q` for a manifold `Q`, indexed by
`i ∈ ℤ/N`. Each generates the cotangent relation `p = d₁S_i(q, Q)`, `P = -d₂S_i(q, Q)`, whose
source and target points are `TauCeti.CotangentBundle.generatingSource` and
`TauCeti.CotangentBundle.generatingTarget`. The **cyclic discrete action**

`A(q_0, …, q_(N-1)) = Σ_i S_i(q_i, q_(i+1))`, indices mod `N`

(`TauCeti.cyclicAction`) is a function on the finite product `ℤ/N → Q`, a manifold for
`ModelWithCorners.pi`. Where each `S_i` is differentiable at `(q_i, q_(i+1))`, its differential is

`dA_q(v) = Σ_i (d₁S_i(q_i, q_(i+1)) + d₂S_(i-1)(q_(i-1), q_i)) (v_i)`

(`TauCeti.mvfderiv_cyclicAction_apply`). So `q` is a critical point of `A` exactly when at every
vertex the outgoing covector of edge `i - 1` equals the incoming covector of edge `i`,
`-d₂S_(i-1)(q_(i-1), q_i) = d₁S_i(q_i, q_(i+1))`; equivalently, the target point of the relation
of `S_(i-1)` over `(q_(i-1), q_i)` is the source point of the relation of `S_i` over
`(q_i, q_(i+1))` (`TauCeti.CotangentBundle.mvfderiv_cyclicAction_eq_zero_iff`). On
configurations in a normed space, `A` has the Fréchet derivative
`v ↦ Σ_i dS_i(q_i, q_(i+1)) (v_i, v_(i+1))` (`TauCeti.hasFDerivAt_cyclicAction`). If each `S_i`
is invariant under a diagonal translation `(x, X) ↦ (x + c, X + c)`, then `A` is invariant under
`q ↦ q + c` (`TauCeti.periodic_cyclicAction`).

Suppose now that, over a set `W_i ⊆ Q × Q`, the relation of `S_i` is the graph of a map `φ_i`
defined on a set `D_i` of covectors: every `z ∈ D_i` has its base pair `(π z, π (φ_i z))` in `W_i`
and `(z, φ_i z)` is the point of the relation over it, and every point of `W_i` is such a base
pair. Then the **chain dictionary** (`TauCeti.CotangentBundle.exists_equiv_periodic_of_generating`)
identifies the cyclic sequences `z_i`, `i ∈ ℤ/N`, with `z_i ∈ D_i` and `φ_i(z_i) = z_(i+1)`, that
is, the phase points fixed by `φ_(N-1) ∘ ⋯ ∘ φ_0` together with their intermediate states, with
the critical points of `A` on the configuration domain `{q | ∀ i, (q_i, q_(i+1)) ∈ W_i}`. The
bijection sends a sequence to its base points, and a critical configuration to the source points
`(q_i, d₁S_i(q_i, q_(i+1)))`. It uses neither finite dimension, nor a boundaryless model, nor the
symplecticity or smoothness of the maps `φ_i`.

Shifting a configuration and the functions together, `q ↦ (i ↦ q (i + k))` and
`S ↦ (i ↦ S (i + k))`, preserves the action (`TauCeti.cyclicAction_comp_add_right`) and its
critical points (`TauCeti.mvfderiv_cyclicAction_comp_add_right_eq_zero_iff`). Iterates are the
case of equal summands `S_i = S`. A periodic chain of a single map `φ` is the orbit of its first
state, so the chain dictionary identifies the points `z` with `φ^[N] z = z` whose iterates
`z, φ z, …, φ^[N-1] z` all lie in `D` with the critical points of `A_N(q) = Σ_i S(q_i, q_(i+1))`,
by `z ↦ (i ↦ π (φ^[i] z))` (`TauCeti.CotangentBundle.exists_equiv_iterate_of_generating`). The
least period of `z` need only divide `N`. Under this bijection the cyclic shift `i ↦ q (i + 1)` of a
critical configuration is the same periodic orbit marked at `φ z`, so the critical configurations
up to cyclic shifts correspond to the periodic orbits without a marked point
(`TauCeti.CotangentBundle.exists_equiv_quot_iterate_of_generating`).

With a single vertex, the differential of `ψ(q) = S(q, q)` is `d₁S(q, q) + d₂S(q, q)`
(`TauCeti.mvfderiv_diag_eq_add`), and the dictionary identifies the fixed points of a map
generated by `S` with the critical points of `ψ`
(`TauCeti.CotangentBundle.exists_equiv_fixedPoints_of_generating`).

## References

* A. Cannas da Silva, *Lectures on Symplectic Geometry*, Lecture Notes in Mathematics 1764,
  Springer, 2001, Section 5.1 (periodic points), Propositions 5.1 and 5.2.
-/

public section

noncomputable section

open Bundle Manifold
open scoped Manifold ContDiff

namespace TauCeti

variable {E H : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [NormedSpace ℝ E] [TopologicalSpace H]
  {I : ModelWithCorners ℝ E H} {Q : Type*} [TopologicalSpace Q] [ChartedSpace H Q]
  {N : ℕ} [NeZero N]

/-- The **cyclic discrete action** `A(q) = Σ_i S_i(q_i, q_(i+1))` of a family of functions
`S_i : Q × Q → ℝ` indexed by `ℤ/N`, on configurations `q : ℤ/N → Q`. -/
def cyclicAction (S : ZMod N → Q × Q → ℝ) (q : ZMod N → Q) : ℝ :=
  ∑ i, S i (q i, q (i + 1))

omit [TopologicalSpace Q] in
/-- The cyclic discrete action is the sum of the generating functions over the edges. -/
theorem cyclicAction_apply (S : ZMod N → Q × Q → ℝ) (q : ZMod N → Q) :
    cyclicAction S q = ∑ i, S i (q i, q (i + 1)) :=
  (rfl)

/-- If each `S_i` is invariant under the diagonal translation `(x, X) ↦ (x + c, X + c)`, then the
cyclic discrete action is invariant under the diagonal translation `q ↦ q + c` of
configurations. -/
theorem periodic_cyclicAction {G : Type*} [Add G] {c : G} {S : ZMod N → G × G → ℝ}
    (hS : ∀ i, Function.Periodic (S i) (c, c)) :
    Function.Periodic (cyclicAction S) fun _ ↦ c := fun q ↦ by
  simp only [cyclicAction_apply, Pi.add_apply]
  exact Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ ↦ by simpa using hS i (q i, q (i + 1))

/-- **The derivative of the cyclic discrete action** on configurations in a normed space. If each
`S_i` is differentiable at the edge `(q_i, q_(i+1))`, then `A(q) = Σ_i S_i(q_i, q_(i+1))` has
derivative `v ↦ Σ_i dS_i(q_i, q_(i+1)) (v_i, v_(i+1))` at `q`. -/
theorem hasFDerivAt_cyclicAction {S : ZMod N → E × E → ℝ} {q : ZMod N → E}
    (hS : ∀ i, DifferentiableAt ℝ (S i) (q i, q (i + 1))) :
    HasFDerivAt (cyclicAction S)
      (∑ i, (fderiv ℝ (S i) (q i, q (i + 1))).comp
        ((ContinuousLinearMap.proj i).prod (ContinuousLinearMap.proj (i + 1)))) q := by
  have h : cyclicAction S = fun q' ↦ ∑ i, S i (q' i, q' (i + 1)) := by
    funext q'
    simp [cyclicAction_apply]
  rw [h]
  exact HasFDerivAt.fun_sum fun i _ ↦ (hS i).hasFDerivAt.comp q
    ((hasFDerivAt_apply i q).prodMk (hasFDerivAt_apply (i + 1) q))

/-- If each `S_i` is differentiable at the edge `(q_i, q_(i+1))`, then the cyclic discrete action
`A(q) = Σ_i S_i(q_i, q_(i+1))` on configurations in a normed space is differentiable at `q`. -/
theorem differentiableAt_cyclicAction {S : ZMod N → E × E → ℝ} {q : ZMod N → E}
    (hS : ∀ i, DifferentiableAt ℝ (S i) (q i, q (i + 1))) :
    DifferentiableAt ℝ (cyclicAction S) q :=
  (hasFDerivAt_cyclicAction hS).differentiableAt

/-- If each `S_i` is `C^n` at the edge `(q_i, q_(i+1))`, then the cyclic discrete action
`A(q) = Σ_i S_i(q_i, q_(i+1))` on configurations in a normed space is `C^n` at `q`. -/
theorem contDiffAt_cyclicAction {n : ℕ∞ω} {S : ZMod N → E × E → ℝ} {q : ZMod N → E}
    (hS : ∀ i, ContDiffAt ℝ n (S i) (q i, q (i + 1))) :
    ContDiffAt ℝ n (cyclicAction S) q := by
  have h : cyclicAction S = fun q' ↦ ∑ i, S i (q' i, q' (i + 1)) := by
    funext q'
    simp [cyclicAction_apply]
  rw [h]
  exact ContDiffAt.sum fun i _ ↦ (hS i).comp q
    ((contDiffAt_apply ℝ (fun _ ↦ E) i q).prodMk (contDiffAt_apply ℝ (fun _ ↦ E) (i + 1) q))

/-- The edge `(q_i, q_(i+1))` of a configuration has derivative `v ↦ (v_i, v_(i+1))`. -/
private theorem hasMFDerivAt_edge (i : ZMod N) (q : ZMod N → Q) :
    HasMFDerivAt (ModelWithCorners.pi fun _ : ZMod N ↦ I) (I.prod I)
      (fun q : ZMod N → Q ↦ (q i, q (i + 1))) q
      ((ContinuousLinearMap.proj i).prod (ContinuousLinearMap.proj (i + 1))) :=
  (hasMFDerivAt_apply (M := fun _ : ZMod N ↦ Q) i q).prodMk
    (hasMFDerivAt_apply (M := fun _ : ZMod N ↦ Q) (i + 1) q)

/-- **The differential of the cyclic discrete action.** If each `S_i` is differentiable at the
edge `(q_i, q_(i+1))`, the differential of `A` at `q` pairs a tangent vector `v` with
`Σ_i (d₁S_i(q_i, q_(i+1)) + d₂S_(i-1)(q_(i-1), q_i)) (v_i)`. -/
theorem mvfderiv_cyclicAction_apply {S : ZMod N → Q × Q → ℝ} {q : ZMod N → Q}
    (hS : ∀ i, MDifferentiableAt (I.prod I) 𝓘(ℝ) (S i) (q i, q (i + 1)))
    (v : ZMod N → E) :
    mvfderiv (ModelWithCorners.pi fun _ : ZMod N ↦ I) (cyclicAction S) q v =
      ∑ i, (mvfderiv I (fun x ↦ S i (x, q (i + 1))) (q i) (v i) +
        mvfderiv I (fun x ↦ S (i - 1) (q (i - 1), x)) (q i) (v i)) := by
  -- Each summand of `A` is `S_i` composed with the edge map, whose differential is
  -- `v ↦ (v_i, v_(i+1))`.
  have hfun : cyclicAction S =
      fun q' ↦ ∑ i, (S i ∘ fun q : ZMod N → Q ↦ (q i, q (i + 1))) q' := by
    ext q'
    simp [cyclicAction_apply]
  have hd : mvfderiv (ModelWithCorners.pi fun _ : ZMod N ↦ I) (cyclicAction S) q v =
      ∑ i, mvfderiv (I.prod I) (S i) (q i, q (i + 1)) (v i, v (i + 1)) := by
    rw [hfun, mvfderiv_fun_sum fun i _ ↦
      (hS i).comp q (hasMFDerivAt_edge (I := I) i q).mdifferentiableAt]
    refine (sum_apply (F := (ZMod N → E) →L[ℝ] ℝ) Finset.univ _ v).trans
      (Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ ↦ ?_)
    refine (mvfderiv_comp_apply q (hS i) (hasMFDerivAt_edge (I := I) i q).mdifferentiableAt
      v).trans ?_
    rw [(hasMFDerivAt_edge (I := I) i q).mfderiv]
    -- The differential `(proj i).prod (proj (i + 1))` of the edge map sends `v` to
    -- `(v i, v (i + 1))`; `simp` cannot rewrite it across the tangent-space type synonyms.
    exact congrArg _ (ContinuousLinearMap.prod_apply _ _ v)
  -- Split each derivative of `S_i` into its two partial derivatives, then shift the index of the
  -- second partial derivative by one.
  rw [hd]
  calc ∑ i, mvfderiv (I.prod I) (S i) (q i, q (i + 1)) (v i, v (i + 1))
      = ∑ i, (mvfderiv I (fun x ↦ S i (x, q (i + 1))) (q i) (v i) +
          mvfderiv I (fun x ↦ S i (q i, x)) (q (i + 1)) (v (i + 1))) :=
        Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ ↦ (hS i).mvfderiv_prod_eq_add_apply (v i, v (i + 1))
    _ = _ := by
        rw [Finset.sum_add_distrib, Finset.sum_add_distrib]
        congr 1
        refine Fintype.sum_equiv (Equiv.addRight 1) _ _ fun i ↦ ?_
        dsimp only [Equiv.coe_addRight]
        simp only [add_sub_cancel_right]

omit [TopologicalSpace Q] in
/-- **The cyclic discrete action is invariant under cyclic shifts.** Shifting the configuration
and the functions by the same `k` does not change the action:
`Σ_i S_(i+k)(q_(i+k), q_(i+k+1)) = Σ_i S_i(q_i, q_(i+1))`. -/
theorem cyclicAction_comp_add_right (S : ZMod N → Q × Q → ℝ) (q : ZMod N → Q) (k : ZMod N) :
    cyclicAction (fun i ↦ S (i + k)) (fun i ↦ q (i + k)) = cyclicAction S q := by
  simp only [cyclicAction_apply]
  exact Fintype.sum_equiv (Equiv.addRight k) _ _ fun i ↦ by simp [add_right_comm]

/-- **Cyclic shifts preserve critical configurations.** A configuration `q` is a critical point of
the cyclic action `Σ_i S_i(q_i, q_(i+1))` exactly when its shift `i ↦ q (i + k)` is a critical
point of the cyclic action of the shifted functions `i ↦ S (i + k)`. With equal summands
`S_i = S`, the cyclic shifts act on the critical configurations of `Σ_i S(q_i, q_(i+1))`. -/
theorem mvfderiv_cyclicAction_comp_add_right_eq_zero_iff (S : ZMod N → Q × Q → ℝ)
    (q : ZMod N → Q) (k : ZMod N) :
    mvfderiv (ModelWithCorners.pi fun _ : ZMod N ↦ I) (cyclicAction fun i ↦ S (i + k))
        (fun i ↦ q (i + k)) = 0 ↔
      mvfderiv (ModelWithCorners.pi fun _ : ZMod N ↦ I) (cyclicAction S) q = 0 := by
  have hcomp : (cyclicAction fun i ↦ S (i + k)) ∘ (fun q : ZMod N → Q ↦ fun i ↦ q (i + k)) =
      cyclicAction S :=
    funext fun q ↦ cyclicAction_comp_add_right S q k
  by_cases hd : MDifferentiableAt (ModelWithCorners.pi fun _ : ZMod N ↦ I) 𝓘(ℝ)
      (cyclicAction fun i ↦ S (i + k)) (fun i ↦ q (i + k))
  · -- The differential of the action at `q` is the differential of the shifted action composed
    -- with the shift of tangent vectors, which is surjective.
    have key (v : ZMod N → E) :
        mvfderiv (ModelWithCorners.pi fun _ : ZMod N ↦ I) (cyclicAction S) q v =
          mvfderiv (ModelWithCorners.pi fun _ : ZMod N ↦ I) (cyclicAction fun i ↦ S (i + k))
            (fun i ↦ q (i + k)) fun i ↦ v (i + k) := by
      rw [← hcomp, mvfderiv_comp_apply q hd
        (hasMFDerivAt_precomp (M := fun _ : ZMod N ↦ Q) (· + k) q).mdifferentiableAt v,
        mfderiv_precomp]
      -- `Pi.compRightL` sends `v` to `i ↦ v (i + k)`; `simp` cannot rewrite it across the
      -- tangent-space type synonyms.
      rfl
    -- In both directions the remaining step evaluates the zero map, which `simp` cannot do across
    -- the tangent-space type synonyms.
    constructor
    · intro h
      exact ContinuousLinearMap.ext fun v ↦ (key v).trans (by rw [h]; rfl)
    · intro h
      refine ContinuousLinearMap.ext fun v ↦ ?_
      have hv := key fun i ↦ v (i - k)
      simp only [add_sub_cancel_right] at hv
      exact hv.symm.trans (by rw [h]; rfl)
  · -- Otherwise neither action is differentiable, since each is the other composed with a shift.
    have hd' : ¬MDifferentiableAt (ModelWithCorners.pi fun _ : ZMod N ↦ I) 𝓘(ℝ)
        (cyclicAction S) q := by
      intro h
      have hinv : (cyclicAction fun i ↦ S (i + k)) =
          cyclicAction S ∘ fun q : ZMod N → Q ↦ fun i ↦ q (i + -k) := by
        funext q'
        rw [Function.comp_apply, ← cyclicAction_comp_add_right S _ k]
        simp only [add_neg_cancel_right]
      rw [hinv] at hd
      exact hd (h.comp_of_eq _
        (hasMFDerivAt_precomp (M := fun _ : ZMod N ↦ Q) (· + -k) _).mdifferentiableAt
        (by simp))
    simp [mvfderiv, mfderiv_zero_of_not_mdifferentiableAt hd,
      mfderiv_zero_of_not_mdifferentiableAt hd']

namespace CotangentBundle

/-- **Critical points of the cyclic discrete action.** If each `S_i` is differentiable at the
edge `(q_i, q_(i+1))`, then `q` is a critical point of `A(q) = Σ_i S_i(q_i, q_(i+1))` exactly
when at every vertex the outgoing covector of edge `i - 1` equals the incoming covector of edge
`i`: the target point `(q_i, -d₂S_(i-1)(q_(i-1), q_i))` of the relation generated by `S_(i-1)`
is the source point `(q_i, d₁S_i(q_i, q_(i+1)))` of the relation generated by `S_i`. -/
theorem mvfderiv_cyclicAction_eq_zero_iff {S : ZMod N → Q × Q → ℝ} {q : ZMod N → Q}
    (hS : ∀ i, MDifferentiableAt (I.prod I) 𝓘(ℝ) (S i) (q i, q (i + 1))) :
    mvfderiv (ModelWithCorners.pi fun _ : ZMod N ↦ I) (cyclicAction S) q = 0 ↔
      ∀ i, generatingTarget I (S (i - 1)) (q (i - 1), q i) =
        generatingSource I (S i) (q i, q (i + 1)) := by
  have key (i : ZMod N) : generatingTarget I (S (i - 1)) (q (i - 1), q i) =
      generatingSource I (S i) (q i, q (i + 1)) ↔
        mvfderiv I (fun x ↦ S i (x, q (i + 1))) (q i) +
          mvfderiv I (fun x ↦ S (i - 1) (q (i - 1), x)) (q i) = 0 := by
    rw [generatingTarget_eq_generatingSource_iff_neg_mvfderiv_eq, neg_eq_iff_add_eq_zero,
      add_comm]
  simp only [key]
  constructor
  · -- Test the vanishing differential on tangent vectors supported at a single vertex. The
    -- covectors are read in `E →L[ℝ] ℝ`, the common type of the cotangent spaces of `Q`.
    have hsingle {A B : ZMod N → E →L[ℝ] ℝ}
        (hAB : ∀ v : ZMod N → E, ∑ i, (A i (v i) + B i (v i)) = 0) (i : ZMod N) :
        A i + B i = 0 := by
      ext w
      have hi := hAB (Pi.single i w)
      rw [Fintype.sum_eq_single i fun j hj ↦ by simp [Pi.single_eq_of_ne hj]] at hi
      simpa using hi
    intro h
    exact hsingle fun v ↦ (mvfderiv_cyclicAction_apply hS v).symm.trans
      (by rw [h]; exact zero_apply v)
  · intro h
    refine ContinuousLinearMap.ext fun v : ZMod N → E ↦ ?_
    rw [mvfderiv_cyclicAction_apply hS]
    refine (Finset.sum_eq_zero fun i _ ↦ ?_).trans (zero_apply v).symm
    -- Evaluate the matching equation at vertex `i` on the component `v_i`.
    exact (add_apply (mvfderiv I (fun x ↦ S i (x, q (i + 1))) (q i))
      (mvfderiv I (fun x ↦ S (i - 1) (q (i - 1), x)) (q i)) (v i)).symm.trans
        ((congrArg (fun L ↦ L (v i)) (h i)).trans
          (zero_apply (F := TangentSpace I (q i) →L[ℝ] ℝ) (v i)))

/-- **The chain dictionary.** Let `S_i`, `i ∈ ℤ/N`, be real functions on `Q × Q`, differentiable on
sets `W_i`, and suppose that over `W_i` the cotangent relation generated by `S_i` is the graph of
a map `φ_i` defined on a set `D_i` of covectors: every `z ∈ D_i` has its base pair
`(π z, π (φ_i z))` in `W_i`, with `(z, φ_i z)` the point of the relation over it, and every point
of `W_i` is such a base pair. Then taking base points is a bijection from the cyclic sequences
`z_i ∈ D_i` with `φ_i(z_i) = z_(i+1)`, the periodic chains of the `φ_i`, onto the critical points
of the cyclic action `Σ_i S_i(q_i, q_(i+1))` on the configurations with every edge
`(q_i, q_(i+1))` in `W_i`. Its inverse sends a critical configuration to the source points
`(q_i, d₁S_i(q_i, q_(i+1)))`. -/
theorem exists_equiv_periodic_of_generating {S : ZMod N → Q × Q → ℝ} {W : ZMod N → Set (Q × Q)}
    {D : ZMod N → Set (CotangentBundle I Q)}
    {φ : ZMod N → CotangentBundle I Q → CotangentBundle I Q}
    (hS : ∀ i, ∀ x ∈ W i, MDifferentiableAt (I.prod I) 𝓘(ℝ) (S i) x)
    (hD : ∀ i, ∀ z ∈ D i, (z.proj, (φ i z).proj) ∈ W i ∧
      generatingCorrespondence I I (S i) (z.proj, (φ i z).proj) = (z, φ i z))
    (hW : ∀ i, ∀ x ∈ W i, ∃ z ∈ D i, (z.proj, (φ i z).proj) = x) :
    ∃ e : {z : ZMod N → CotangentBundle I Q // ∀ i, z i ∈ D i ∧ φ i (z i) = z (i + 1)} ≃
        {q : ZMod N → Q // (∀ i, (q i, q (i + 1)) ∈ W i) ∧
          mvfderiv (ModelWithCorners.pi fun _ : ZMod N ↦ I) (cyclicAction S) q = 0},
      (∀ z i, (e z : ZMod N → Q) i = (z.val i).proj) ∧
        ∀ q i, (e.symm q : ZMod N → CotangentBundle I Q) i =
          generatingSource I (S i) (q.val i, q.val (i + 1)) := by
  -- Along a periodic chain, each state is the source point and the next state the target point
  -- of the relation over the base pair of consecutive states.
  have hchain (z : ZMod N → CotangentBundle I Q) (hz : ∀ i, z i ∈ D i ∧ φ i (z i) = z (i + 1))
      (i : ZMod N) : ((z i).proj, (z (i + 1)).proj) ∈ W i ∧
        generatingSource I (S i) ((z i).proj, (z (i + 1)).proj) = z i ∧
        generatingTarget I (S i) ((z i).proj, (z (i + 1)).proj) = z (i + 1) := by
    have h := hD i _ (hz i).1
    rw [(hz i).2, generatingCorrespondence_apply, Prod.mk.injEq] at h
    exact ⟨h.1, h.2⟩
  -- Over each edge of a configuration in the domain, the source point lies in `D_i` and `φ_i`
  -- sends it to the target point.
  have hedge (i : ZMod N) (x : Q × Q) (hx : x ∈ W i) :
      generatingSource I (S i) x ∈ D i ∧
        φ i (generatingSource I (S i) x) = generatingTarget I (S i) x := by
    obtain ⟨z, hz, rfl⟩ := hW i x hx
    have h := (hD i z hz).2
    rw [generatingCorrespondence_apply, Prod.mk.injEq] at h
    rw [h.1, h.2]
    exact ⟨hz, rfl⟩
  refine ⟨
    { toFun := fun z ↦ ⟨fun i ↦ (z.val i).proj, fun i ↦ (hchain z.val z.property i).1,
        (mvfderiv_cyclicAction_eq_zero_iff fun i ↦ hS i _ (hchain z.val z.property i).1).2 fun i ↦
            by
          have h := (hchain z.val z.property (i - 1)).2.2
          rw [sub_add_cancel] at h
          rw [h, (hchain z.val z.property i).2.1]⟩
      invFun := fun q ↦ ⟨fun i ↦ generatingSource I (S i) (q.val i, q.val (i + 1)), fun i ↦ by
        refine ⟨(hedge i _ (q.property.1 i)).1, (hedge i _ (q.property.1 i)).2.trans ?_⟩
        have h := (mvfderiv_cyclicAction_eq_zero_iff fun i ↦ hS i _ (q.property.1 i)).1 q.property.2
            (i + 1)
        rwa [add_sub_cancel_right] at h⟩
      left_inv := fun z ↦ Subtype.ext <| funext fun i ↦ (hchain z.val z.property i).2.1
      right_inv := fun q ↦ Subtype.ext <| funext fun i ↦ proj_generatingSource _ },
    fun _ _ ↦ rfl, fun _ _ ↦ rfl⟩

/-- **Fixed points and critical points.** Suppose that over a set `W ⊆ Q × Q`, on which `S` is
differentiable, the cotangent relation generated by `S` is the graph of a map `φ` defined on a set
`D` of covectors, as in `exists_equiv_periodic_of_generating`. Then taking base points is a
bijection from the fixed points of `φ` in `D` onto the critical points of `ψ(q) = S(q, q)` on
`{q | (q, q) ∈ W}`, with inverse `q ↦ (q, d₁S(q, q))`. This is the chain dictionary with a single
vertex. -/
theorem exists_equiv_fixedPoints_of_generating {S : Q × Q → ℝ} {W : Set (Q × Q)}
    {D : Set (CotangentBundle I Q)} {φ : CotangentBundle I Q → CotangentBundle I Q}
    (hS : ∀ x ∈ W, MDifferentiableAt (I.prod I) 𝓘(ℝ) S x)
    (hD : ∀ z ∈ D, (z.proj, (φ z).proj) ∈ W ∧
      generatingCorrespondence I I S (z.proj, (φ z).proj) = (z, φ z))
    (hW : ∀ x ∈ W, ∃ z ∈ D, (z.proj, (φ z).proj) = x) :
    ∃ e : {z : CotangentBundle I Q // z ∈ D ∧ φ z = z} ≃
        {q : Q // (q, q) ∈ W ∧ mvfderiv I (fun x ↦ S (x, x)) q = 0},
      (∀ z, (e z : Q) = z.val.proj) ∧
        ∀ q, (e.symm q : CotangentBundle I Q) = generatingSource I S (q.val, q.val) := by
  obtain ⟨e, he, he'⟩ := exists_equiv_periodic_of_generating (N := 1) (S := fun _ ↦ S)
    (W := fun _ ↦ W) (D := fun _ ↦ D) (φ := fun _ ↦ φ) (fun _ ↦ hS) (fun _ ↦ hD) (fun _ ↦ hW)
  -- A constant configuration is critical for the cyclic action exactly when its value is
  -- critical for `ψ`: both say that the target and source points over `(q, q)` agree.
  have hcrit (q : Q) (hq : (q, q) ∈ W) :
      mvfderiv (ModelWithCorners.pi fun _ : ZMod 1 ↦ I) (cyclicAction (N := 1) fun _ ↦ S)
          (fun _ ↦ q) = 0 ↔ mvfderiv I (fun x ↦ S (x, x)) q = 0 := by
    rw [mvfderiv_cyclicAction_eq_zero_iff (N := 1) (S := fun _ ↦ S) (q := fun _ ↦ q)
        fun _ ↦ hS _ hq, mvfderiv_diag_eq_add (hS _ hq),
      add_comm, ← neg_eq_iff_add_eq_zero]
    simp only [generatingTarget_eq_generatingSource_iff_neg_mvfderiv_eq, forall_const]
  -- On `ℤ/1` every index is the default one, so a function on `ℤ/1` is its value there and the
  -- successor of every index is itself.
  have h1 (i : ZMod 1) : i + 1 = i := Subsingleton.elim _ _
  let e₁ : {z : ZMod 1 → CotangentBundle I Q // ∀ i, z i ∈ D ∧ φ (z i) = z (i + 1)} ≃
      {z : CotangentBundle I Q // z ∈ D ∧ φ z = z} :=
    (Equiv.funUnique (ZMod 1) _).subtypeEquiv fun z ↦ by
      simp only [Equiv.funUnique_apply, Unique.forall_iff, h1]
  let e₂ : {q : ZMod 1 → Q // (∀ i, (q i, q (i + 1)) ∈ W) ∧
        mvfderiv (ModelWithCorners.pi fun _ : ZMod 1 ↦ I) (cyclicAction (N := 1) fun _ ↦ S) q = 0} ≃
      {q : Q // (q, q) ∈ W ∧ mvfderiv I (fun x ↦ S (x, x)) q = 0} :=
    (Equiv.funUnique (ZMod 1) _).subtypeEquiv fun q ↦ by
      obtain ⟨x, rfl⟩ : ∃ x, q = fun _ ↦ x :=
        ⟨q default, funext fun i ↦ congrArg q (Unique.eq_default i)⟩
      simp only [Equiv.funUnique_apply, forall_const]
      exact and_congr_right (hcrit x)
  exact ⟨e₁.symm.trans (e.trans e₂), fun z ↦ he _ 0, fun q ↦ he' _ 0⟩

/-- **Iterates and critical points.** Suppose that over a set `W ⊆ Q × Q`, on which `S` is
differentiable, the cotangent relation generated by `S` is the graph of a map `φ` defined on a set
`D` of covectors, as in `exists_equiv_periodic_of_generating`. Then taking base points along the
orbit is a bijection `e` from the points `z` of period `N` of `φ` whose iterates
`z, φ z, …, φ^[N-1] z` lie in `D` onto the critical points of
`A_N(q) = Σ_i S(q_i, q_(i+1))` on the configurations with every edge `(q_i, q_(i+1))` in `W`: it
sends `z` to `i ↦ π (φ^[i] z)`, and its inverse sends `q` to the source point
`(q_0, d₁S(q_0, q_1))`. The least period of `z` need only divide `N`.

A cyclic shift of a critical configuration is the same periodic orbit with another marked point:
`e z'` is the shift `i ↦ e z (i + 1)` of `e z` exactly when `z' = φ z`. -/
theorem exists_equiv_iterate_of_generating {S : Q × Q → ℝ} {W : Set (Q × Q)}
    {D : Set (CotangentBundle I Q)} {φ : CotangentBundle I Q → CotangentBundle I Q}
    (hS : ∀ x ∈ W, MDifferentiableAt (I.prod I) 𝓘(ℝ) S x)
    (hD : ∀ z ∈ D, (z.proj, (φ z).proj) ∈ W ∧
      generatingCorrespondence I I S (z.proj, (φ z).proj) = (z, φ z))
    (hW : ∀ x ∈ W, ∃ z ∈ D, (z.proj, (φ z).proj) = x) :
    ∃ e : {z : CotangentBundle I Q // (∀ k < N, φ^[k] z ∈ D) ∧ Function.IsPeriodicPt φ N z} ≃
        {q : ZMod N → Q // (∀ i, (q i, q (i + 1)) ∈ W) ∧
          mvfderiv (ModelWithCorners.pi fun _ : ZMod N ↦ I) (cyclicAction fun _ ↦ S) q = 0},
      (∀ z i, (e z : ZMod N → Q) i = (φ^[i.val] z.val).proj) ∧
      (∀ q, (e.symm q : CotangentBundle I Q) = generatingSource I S (q.val 0, q.val 1)) ∧
      ∀ z z', ((e z' : ZMod N → Q) = fun i ↦ (e z : ZMod N → Q) (i + 1)) ↔ z'.val = φ z.val := by
  obtain ⟨e, he, he'⟩ := exists_equiv_periodic_of_generating (N := N) (S := fun _ ↦ S)
    (W := fun _ ↦ W) (D := fun _ ↦ D) (φ := fun _ ↦ φ) (fun _ ↦ hS) (fun _ ↦ hD) (fun _ ↦ hW)
  refine ⟨(Function.periodicChainEquiv φ D N).symm.trans e, fun z i ↦ ?_, fun q ↦ ?_,
    fun z z' ↦ ?_⟩
  · simp [he]
  · simp [he']
  -- Pass to the periodic chains `w = c⁻¹ z`, `w' = c⁻¹ z'`, on which the shift of base points is
  -- the shift of the chains, since a chain is recovered from its base points.
  obtain ⟨w, rfl⟩ := (Function.periodicChainEquiv φ D N).surjective z
  obtain ⟨w', rfl⟩ := (Function.periodicChainEquiv φ D N).surjective z'
  rw [Function.coe_periodicChainEquiv_eq_iff]
  simp only [Equiv.trans_apply, Equiv.symm_apply_apply]
  constructor
  · intro h
    funext i
    have hw' := congrFun (congrArg Subtype.val (e.symm_apply_apply w')) i
    have hw := congrFun (congrArg Subtype.val (e.symm_apply_apply w)) (i + 1)
    simp only [he'] at hw' hw
    rw [← hw', ← hw, h]
  · intro h
    funext i
    simp [he, h]

/-- **Unmarked periodic orbits and critical configurations up to cyclic shifts.** Under the
hypotheses of `exists_equiv_iterate_of_generating`, the periodic orbits of `φ` through points of
period `N` whose iterates lie in `D`, without a marked point, correspond to the critical points of
`A_N(q) = Σ_i S(q_i, q_(i+1))` on its configuration domain up to cyclic shifts: the quotients by
`z ↦ φ z` and by `q ↦ (i ↦ q (i + 1))` are in bijection, sending the class of `z` to the class of
its configuration of base points `i ↦ π (φ^[i] z)`. -/
theorem exists_equiv_quot_iterate_of_generating {S : Q × Q → ℝ} {W : Set (Q × Q)}
    {D : Set (CotangentBundle I Q)} {φ : CotangentBundle I Q → CotangentBundle I Q}
    (hS : ∀ x ∈ W, MDifferentiableAt (I.prod I) 𝓘(ℝ) S x)
    (hD : ∀ z ∈ D, (z.proj, (φ z).proj) ∈ W ∧
      generatingCorrespondence I I S (z.proj, (φ z).proj) = (z, φ z))
    (hW : ∀ x ∈ W, ∃ z ∈ D, (z.proj, (φ z).proj) = x) :
    ∃ e : Quot (fun z z' : {z : CotangentBundle I Q //
          (∀ k < N, φ^[k] z ∈ D) ∧ Function.IsPeriodicPt φ N z} ↦ z'.val = φ z.val) ≃
        Quot (fun q q' : {q : ZMod N → Q // (∀ i, (q i, q (i + 1)) ∈ W) ∧
          mvfderiv (ModelWithCorners.pi fun _ : ZMod N ↦ I) (cyclicAction fun _ ↦ S) q = 0} ↦
            q'.val = fun i ↦ q.val (i + 1)),
      ∀ z q, (∀ i, q.val i = (φ^[i.val] z.val).proj) → e (Quot.mk _ z) = Quot.mk _ q := by
  obtain ⟨e, he, -, hshift⟩ := exists_equiv_iterate_of_generating (N := N) hS hD hW
  refine ⟨Quot.congr e fun z z' ↦ (hshift z z').symm, fun z q hq ↦ ?_⟩
  rw [Quot.congr_mk]
  congr
  exact Subtype.ext <| funext fun i ↦ (he z i).trans (hq i).symm

end CotangentBundle

end TauCeti
